# Line endings are load-bearing: the gate script and the pre-push hook are the only
# thing standing between a red gate and main, and `sh tools/gate.sh` must not depend
# on how git checked the file out on Windows. core.autocrlf=true is the default on
# Windows, so the catch-all below is what keeps a clone and CI byte-identical.
* text eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# README screenshots must survive byte-for-byte.
*.png binary
